# Corpses of the Lost: "if you descended this turn" needs a PERMANENT CARD put into your graveyard (CR 700.11). Turn 1
# Bot1 casts it, then Lightning Bolt at its own Skeleton Pirate (a 3/2): the token dies (a token is not a card, so it does not
# count, CR 111.7) and the Bolt, an instant, goes to the graveyard (not a permanent card). Bot1 has not descended, so the
# trigger is never put on the stack and nothing asks for a payment (the refusal); the scenario where a discarded
# Ornithopter does make it ask is the positive control. Life stays at 20 and the enchantment stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Corpses of the Lost
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Mountain
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Corpses of the Lost.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Skeleton Pirate Token)
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Accept
[T2 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Corpses of the Lost.Types = Enchantment
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter
